## 4. How Results Will Be Measured and Verified

Every phase below must satisfy these checks before being considered done. This mirrors the project's existing determinism/evidence discipline — no new verification philosophy, only applying the existing one to more assets.

### 4.1 Correctness checks (per asset added)
- [ ] Dataset loads with the correct `record_count`, `start_time`, `end_time` (spot-checked against source CSV).
- [ ] `BacktestEngine.run()` produces a `result_hash` that is **stable across repeated runs** on identical input (determinism check — already proven for XAUUSD, must be repeated per asset).
- [ ] Annualized metrics (Sharpe, volatility) use the correct `periods_per_year` for that asset's class once the Instrument Metadata Registry (3.2) exists — verified against a manually computed reference value for at least one asset per class (equity, FX/metals, crypto).

### 4.2 Cross-asset consistency checks
- [ ] Running the same strategy against two different assets must **not** silently reuse cached state from the first run (isolation check).
- [ ] Batch/sweep runner (3.4) output count must equal `len(symbols) × len(strategies)` exactly — no silently dropped combinations.
- [ ] Each result in the batch must carry a distinct `input_hash` (proves no accidental data leakage between assets).

### 4.3 Evidence integrity checks
- [ ] Every backtest run produces exactly one `EvidenceRecord` with `dataset_reference`, `method`, `result`, `why` populated (not just a console print).
- [ ] `EvidenceRepository` query by symbol returns all and only the evidence for that symbol.
- [ ] Reproduction Engine (`researchos/evidence/reproduction.py`) can regenerate a byte-identical result from a stored `EvidenceRecord` for at least one multi-asset case.

### 4.4 Regression checks (must stay green throughout)
- [ ] Full existing test suite (3,475 Python + 526 C++ tests, per `MACRO_OWNERSHIP_PROPOSAL.md` baseline) remains green after each phase.
- [ ] `test_bridge.py::TestBacktest` (10/10) and `test_experiment_backend_integration.py::TestBacktestArtifacts` (2/2) remain green — these are the load-bearing tests for this entire plan.
- [ ] XAUUSD backtest result (`result_hash` from the first real run this session) remains reproducible byte-for-byte — this is the regression baseline for "did multi-asset work break the original asset."

